IMPORT prelude

-- Bankruptcy Act 1966 (Commonwealth) -- Part IX, debt agreements: who may give a debt agreement proposal (s 185C(1), (4), (5)
-- "threshold amount"); how long the payments may run (s 185C(2AA)-(2AC)); the Official Receiver's gate (s 185E(2), (2AA), (3)); the
-- applicable deadline (s 185); the creditors' vote (s 185EC) and lapse (s 185G(b)); when the agreement is made (s 185H); what a
-- creditor may do while the proposal is processed (s 185F) and while the agreement is in force (s 185K); proportionate payment
-- (s 185C(2)(d), (e)); the 3-month and designated 6-month arrears defaults (ss 185LB(3), 185LC(3)) and termination for the latter
-- (s 185QA); a variation's time limit (s 185M(1D)-(1DB)); the end of the agreement (s 185N(1), (2)) and the release from debts
-- (s 185NA, read with s 153(2)).
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 97, compilation date 21 May 2026 (includes amendments up to Act No. 47, 2026), Federal Register of
-- Legislation register id C2026C00215, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C1966A00033.txt.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0022 in subjects/au/requirements.jsonl (priority 1), raised 3 times by the Western Australian
-- cradle-to-grave life of Jake Harding (workbench scenarios/au/wa/cradle-to-grave-jake): k065 (2037-04-20, aged 30, debts of
-- $41,000, a creditor's petition threatened; "Who may propose a debt agreement; who decides; what does it do to the debts?"), k066
-- (2037-06-01, "A five-year plan: $690 a month to the administrator", Part IX Division 3) and k075 (2042-05-31, the agreement
-- completes; "What stays on the National Personal Insolvency Index and the credit file, and for how long?", s 185N). The ledger
-- lists ss 185C, 185EC, 185H, Part IX Division 3, s 185N and the Index. SCOPED to those questions, with the definitions,
-- conditions and exceptions needed to answer them.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the s 185C(4)(e) payment-to-income formula -- the deposit prints "the amount worked out using the following formula"
-- and then no formula (it was an image in the source), so whether it exceeds the Minister's percentage is an INPUT; every amount the
-- Act leaves to another instrument is an INPUT: the threshold amount (7 times a rate in the Social Security Act 1991, point 1064-B1,
-- which changes by indexation), any greater amount prescribed by regulations, the Minister's percentage and the low income debtor
-- amount (s 185C(4B)); the content and retention of the National Personal Insolvency Index, which the Act leaves wholly to
-- regulations (s 5 "means the Index of that name established under the regulations"; s 315(2)(a)-(c)); the credit file (Privacy
-- Act 1988 Part IIIA, a separate subject); the approved forms, statement of affairs (s 185D) and explanatory statement contents;
-- cancellation of acceptance (s 185ED); voting on variations and terminations (ss 185MA-185PD); termination by the Court (s 185Q)
-- beyond a comment; voiding (ss 185T-185V); administrators' duties, registration and remuneration (Division 3A, Part IX Division 8
-- and Part IXA beyond what is quoted); s 185EC(3) (assigned debts of a related entity of the debtor); Part X personal insolvency
-- agreements; and bankruptcy itself.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT for public use. See NOTES.md.

§ `Bankruptcy Act 1966 Part IX -- debt agreements`

§§ `helpers`

-- A date is given as year, month and day and compared by a single key.
GIVEN `year` IS A NUMBER, `month` IS A NUMBER, `day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`date key` MEANS `year` TIMES 10000 PLUS `month` TIMES 100 PLUS `day`

GIVEN `first amount` IS A NUMBER, `second amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the higher of` MEANS
    IF `first amount` GREATER THAN `second amount` THEN `first amount` ELSE `second amount`

-- "N years beginning on the day the agreement is made" ends at the end of the day before the Nth anniversary, so a payment falls
-- after that period if it is due on or after the anniversary. (Inference from the words; a 29 February start is not handled.)
GIVEN `made year` IS A NUMBER, `made month` IS A NUMBER, `made day` IS A NUMBER,
      `last year` IS A NUMBER, `last month` IS A NUMBER, `last day` IS A NUMBER, `years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the last payment falls after the period of years` IF
    `date key` `last year` `last month` `last day` AT LEAST `date key` (`made year` PLUS `years`) `made month` `made day`

§§ `185C(2AB) -- the debtor's home`

-- s 185C(2AB): applies "if at the time the debtor gives the debt agreement proposal ... the debtor has an interest in real property
-- in Australia that is a dwelling and is the debtor's principal place of residence, being an interest: (a) that is an interest under
-- a long-term lease; or (b) that is any other legal or equitable estate or interest, except: (i) an interest under a lease (other
-- than a long-term lease); or (ii) an interest under a licence; or (iii) a life interest; or (iv) an interest in an easement; or (v)
-- an interest held on trust for another person; or (vi) an interest of a kind determined in an instrument under subsection (2AD)".
-- s 185C(5): "long-term lease means a lease granted by the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory for a term ... reasonably likely ...
-- to exceed 20 years"; "lease includes a sublease".
DECLARE `Home interest` IS ONE OF
    `no interest in a dwelling`
    `a lease other than a long-term lease`
    `a long-term lease`
    `a licence`
    `a life interest`
    `an interest in an easement`
    `an interest held on trust for another person`
    `a kind determined by the Minister's instrument`
    `any other legal or equitable estate or interest`

GIVEN `the interest` IS A `Home interest`, `a dwelling in Australia that is the principal place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `subsection 185C(2AB) applies` IF
        `a dwelling in Australia that is the principal place of residence`
    AND CONSIDER `the interest`
        WHEN `a long-term lease` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `any other legal or equitable estate or interest` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `185C(1), (4), (5) -- who may give a proposal`

-- s 185C(1): "A debtor who is insolvent may give the Official Receiver a written proposal for a debt agreement." s 5(3): "A person
-- who is not solvent is insolvent"; (2): solvent "if, and only if, the person is able to pay all the person's debts, as and when
-- they become due and payable".
-- s 185C(4): a debtor CANNOT give a proposal if (a) in the 10 years before, the debtor "has been a bankrupt", "has been a party (as
-- debtor) to a debt agreement" or "has given an authority under section 188"; (b) unsecured debts total more than "the threshold
-- amount" or, "if the regulations prescribe a greater amount", that amount; (c) divisible property "is more than twice the threshold
-- amount"; (d) after tax income in the year beginning at the proposal time "is likely to exceed three-quarters of the threshold
-- amount"; or (e) if (2AB) does not apply, the formula percentage exceeds the Minister's percentage "(unless subsection (4C) applies
-- to the debtor)". (4A): (a)(i) does not apply to a bankruptcy annulled under s 153B. (4C) applies if the formula exceeds and the
-- proposed administrator certifies the debtor "is likely to be able to discharge the obligations ... as and when they fall due".
-- s 185C(2E): "A debt agreement proposal must not be given jointly by 2 or more debtors."
-- s 185C(5): "threshold amount ... means 7 times the amount that, at that time, is specified in column 3, item 2, Table B, point
-- 1064-B1, Pension Rate Calculator A, in the Social Security Act 1991". "unsecured debt includes the amount by which the value of a
-- debt exceeds the value of a security given for the debt."
DECLARE Debtor HAS
    `is insolvent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was a bankrupt in the previous 10 years` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that bankruptcy was annulled under s 153B` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was a party as debtor to a debt agreement in the previous 10 years` IS A BOOLEAN
    `gave an authority under s 188 in the previous 10 years` IS A BOOLEAN
    `unsecured debts` IS A NUMBER
    `property divisible among creditors if bankrupt` IS A NUMBER
    `likely after tax income in the next year` IS A NUMBER
    `interest in the home` IS A `Home interest`
    `the home is a dwelling in Australia and the principal place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the s 185C(4)(e) formula exceeds the Minister's percentage` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the proposed administrator gave a s 185C(4C)(b) certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `gives the proposal jointly with another debtor` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the Social Security Act rate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the threshold amount` MEANS 7 TIMES `the Social Security Act rate`

GIVEN `the debtor` IS A Debtor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `subsection 185C(2AB) applies to the debtor` IF
    `subsection 185C(2AB) applies` (`the debtor`'s `interest in the home`) (`the debtor`'s `the home is a dwelling in Australia and the principal place of residence`)

GIVEN `the debtor` IS A Debtor, `threshold` IS A NUMBER, `prescribed greater amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 185C(4) bars the proposal` IF
        (`the debtor`'s `was a bankrupt in the previous 10 years` AND (NOT `the debtor`'s `that bankruptcy was annulled under s 153B`))
    OR  `the debtor`'s `was a party as debtor to a debt agreement in the previous 10 years`
    OR  `the debtor`'s `gave an authority under s 188 in the previous 10 years`
    OR  `the debtor`'s `unsecured debts` GREATER THAN `the higher of` `threshold` `prescribed greater amount`
    OR  `the debtor`'s `property divisible among creditors if bankrupt` GREATER THAN 2 TIMES `threshold`
    OR  `the debtor`'s `likely after tax income in the next year` GREATER THAN `threshold` TIMES 3 DIVIDED BY 4
    OR  (    (NOT `subsection 185C(2AB) applies to the debtor` `the debtor`)
         AND `the debtor`'s `the s 185C(4)(e) formula exceeds the Minister's percentage`
         AND (NOT `the debtor`'s `the proposed administrator gave a s 185C(4C)(b) certificate`))

GIVEN `the debtor` IS A Debtor, `threshold` IS A NUMBER, `prescribed greater amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the debtor may give a debt agreement proposal` IF
        `the debtor`'s `is insolvent`
    AND (NOT `s 185C(4) bars the proposal` `the debtor` `threshold` `prescribed greater amount`)
    AND (NOT `the debtor`'s `gives the proposal jointly with another debtor`)

§§ `185C(2AA), (2AC) -- how long the payments may run`

-- s 185C(2AA): a proposal "must not provide for the debtor to make payments under the agreement, in respect of provable debts ...,
-- after: (a) 3 years beginning on the day the agreement is made; or (b) if subsection (2AB) applies to the debtor -- 5 years".
-- (2AC): if the payments run after 3 but not after 5 years, the property to be dealt with "must not include any interest covered by
-- subsection (2AB)".
GIVEN `the home rule applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most years payments may run` MEANS IF `the home rule applies` THEN 5 ELSE 3

DECLARE Proposal HAS
    `the proposing debtor` IS A Debtor
    `year the agreement would be made` IS A NUMBER
    `month the agreement would be made` IS A NUMBER
    `day the agreement would be made` IS A NUMBER
    `year of the last payment` IS A NUMBER
    `month of the last payment` IS A NUMBER
    `day of the last payment` IS A NUMBER
    `the property to be dealt with includes the home interest` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the other requirements of s 185C(2), (2A), (2B), (2D) and (2DA) are met` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days from signing to giving it to the Official Receiver` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the proposal` IS A Proposal, `years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposal's payments run after` IF
    `the last payment falls after the period of years`
        (`the proposal`'s `year the agreement would be made`) (`the proposal`'s `month the agreement would be made`) (`the proposal`'s `day the agreement would be made`)
        (`the proposal`'s `year of the last payment`) (`the proposal`'s `month of the last payment`) (`the proposal`'s `day of the last payment`)
        `years`

GIVEN `the proposal` IS A Proposal
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the payment term complies with s 185C(2AA) and (2AC)` IF
        (NOT `the proposal's payments run after` `the proposal` (`the most years payments may run` (`subsection 185C(2AB) applies to the debtor` (`the proposal`'s `the proposing debtor`))))
    AND (    (NOT `the proposal's payments run after` `the proposal` 3)
          OR (NOT `the proposal`'s `the property to be dealt with includes the home interest`))

§§ `185E -- the Official Receiver's gate`

-- s 185E(2): the Official Receiver "may accept the proposal for processing if (a) the Official Receiver is satisfied that subsections
-- 185C(2), (2AA), (2AC), (2A), (2B), (2D), (2DA), (2E) and (4) have been complied with; ... (e) ... the statement of affairs ... is in
-- order". (2AA): "must not accept ... unless the proposal was given ... within 14 days after the day on which the debtor signed the
-- proposal". (2AB): "may refuse ... if the Official Receiver reasonably believes that complying with the agreement would cause undue
-- hardship to the debtor". (3): "must not accept ... if the Official Receiver thinks that the creditors' interests would be better
-- served by not accepting". (4): review by the Administrative Review Tribunal.
-- The gate is the Official Receiver's; the decision on the merits is the creditors' (s 185EC). The undue-hardship refusal is a
-- discretion and is not encoded as a bar.
GIVEN `the proposal` IS A Proposal, `threshold` IS A NUMBER, `prescribed greater amount` IS A NUMBER,
      `the Official Receiver thinks creditors are better served by not accepting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Official Receiver may accept the proposal for processing` IF
        `the debtor may give a debt agreement proposal` (`the proposal`'s `the proposing debtor`) `threshold` `prescribed greater amount`
    AND `the payment term complies with s 185C(2AA) and (2AC)` `the proposal`
    AND `the proposal`'s `the other requirements of s 185C(2), (2A), (2B), (2D) and (2DA) are met`
    AND `the proposal`'s `days from signing to giving it to the Official Receiver` AT MOST 14
    AND (NOT `the Official Receiver thinks creditors are better served by not accepting`)

§§ `185 -- the applicable deadline`

-- s 185 "applicable deadline: (a) in relation to a debt agreement proposal, means: (i) if Official Receiver accepted the proposal for
-- processing in December -- the end of the 42nd day after the acceptance; or (ii) otherwise -- the end of the 35th day after".
GIVEN `accepted for processing in December` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`days after acceptance for processing to the applicable deadline` MEANS
    IF `accepted for processing in December` THEN 42 ELSE 35

§§ `185EC, 185G(b) -- the creditors' vote`

-- s 185EC(1): "A debt agreement proposal is accepted if: (a) the Official Receiver writes to affected creditors ...; and (b) a
-- majority in value of the creditors who reply before the applicable deadline state that the proposal should be accepted." (1A):
-- disregard an affected creditor who "is the proposed administrator" or "was, on becoming an affected creditor, a related entity of
-- the proposed administrator". (2): "taken to be accepted at the applicable deadline". (4): value "assessed as at the time when the
-- acceptance ... for processing was recorded on the National Personal Insolvency Index". (5): "a secured creditor is taken to be a
-- creditor only to the extent (if any) by which the amount of the debt owing to the creditor exceeds the value of the creditor's
-- security".
-- s 185G: the proposal lapses if "(b) the Official Receiver accepts the proposal for processing and writes to affected creditors
-- about it, but no replies are received before the applicable deadline".
-- "Majority" is read as more than half of the value of the counted replies; a tie is not a majority.
DECLARE Creditor HAS
    `debt owing when acceptance for processing was recorded` IS A NUMBER
    `value of the creditor's security` IS A NUMBER
    `is the proposed administrator or was its related entity on becoming a creditor` IS A BOOLEAN
    `replied before the applicable deadline` IS A BOOLEAN
    `stated the proposal should be accepted` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the creditor` IS A Creditor
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the value of the creditor` MEANS
    IF `the creditor`'s `debt owing when acceptance for processing was recorded` GREATER THAN `the creditor`'s `value of the creditor's security`
    THEN `the creditor`'s `debt owing when acceptance for processing was recorded` MINUS `the creditor`'s `value of the creditor's security`
    ELSE 0

GIVEN `the creditor` IS A Creditor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the creditor's reply counts` IF
        `the creditor`'s `replied before the applicable deadline`
    AND (NOT `the creditor`'s `is the proposed administrator or was its related entity on becoming a creditor`)

GIVEN `the creditors` IS A LIST OF Creditor
GIVETH A NUMBER
`value of counted replies` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the creditors`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN `one creditor` FOLLOWED BY `the others` THEN
        (IF `the creditor's reply counts` `one creditor` THEN `the value of the creditor` `one creditor` ELSE 0)
        PLUS `value of counted replies` `the others`

GIVEN `the creditors` IS A LIST OF Creditor
GIVETH A NUMBER
`value of counted replies in favour` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the creditors`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN `one creditor` FOLLOWED BY `the others` THEN
        (IF `the creditor's reply counts` `one creditor` AND `one creditor`'s `stated the proposal should be accepted`
         THEN `the value of the creditor` `one creditor` ELSE 0)
        PLUS `value of counted replies in favour` `the others`

GIVEN `the creditors` IS A LIST OF Creditor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `any creditor replied` IF
    CONSIDER `the creditors`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
    WHEN `one creditor` FOLLOWED BY `the others` THEN
        `one creditor`'s `replied before the applicable deadline` OR `any creditor replied` `the others`

DECLARE `Vote outcome` IS ONE OF
    `the proposal is accepted`
    `the proposal is not accepted`
    `the proposal lapses`

GIVEN `the creditors` IS A LIST OF Creditor
GIVETH A `Vote outcome`
`the outcome of the vote` MEANS
    IF NOT `any creditor replied` `the creditors`
    THEN `the proposal lapses`
    ELSE IF 2 TIMES `value of counted replies in favour` `the creditors` GREATER THAN `value of counted replies` `the creditors`
         THEN `the proposal is accepted`
         ELSE `the proposal is not accepted`

§§ `185H -- when the agreement is made`

-- s 185H(2): if a proposal is accepted and is not conditional, "the Official Receiver must enter details of the debt agreement ... on
-- the National Personal Insolvency Index; and (d) the debt agreement is made in the terms of the proposal when those details are so
-- entered". (3): a conditional proposal likewise, but only if "the event occurs within that period". s 185C(2F): the period "must not
-- be longer than 7 days". s 185I: the parties are the debtor and "the creditors to whom the debtor owed provable debts" -- including
-- those who voted no.
GIVEN `accepted` IS A BOOLEAN, `conditional` IS A BOOLEAN, `the event occurred within the period` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `details entered on the Index` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a debt agreement is made` IF
        `accepted`
    AND `details entered on the Index`
    AND ((NOT `conditional`) OR `the event occurred within the period`)

§§ `185F, 185K -- what a creditor may do`

-- s 185 "frozen debt" is a debt owed by a debtor whose proposal has been accepted for processing that "would be a provable debt ...
-- but does not include a debt arising under a maintenance agreement or maintenance order". s 5: "maintenance order" includes "(b) an
-- assessment made under the Child Support (Assessment) Act 1989".
-- s 185F(1), from the recording of acceptance for processing until the deadline or the agreement: (a) a creditor cannot "enforce, a
-- remedy against the debtor's person or property in respect of a frozen debt"; (b) a sheriff must not execute process to enforce
-- payment of a frozen debt; (c) a person entitled to retain or deduct money owing to the debtor "must not retain or deduct money".
-- (2): a creditor may still start a legal proceeding or take a fresh step "(except to enforce a judgment)". (3): proceeds of crime
-- liabilities may be enforced.
-- s 185K(1): while the agreement is in force and on the Index, a creditor cannot (a) present a creditor's petition, (b) proceed with
-- one already presented, or "(c) enforce a remedy against the debtor's person or property, or start or take a fresh step in legal
-- proceedings, in respect of a provable debt". (2): (1)(c) does not prevent enforcing a remedy for "(a) a maintenance agreement; (b)
-- a maintenance order; (c) a proceeds of crime law". (3): "(a) a sheriff must not ... enforce payment of a provable debt ...; and (b)
-- a person who is entitled under a law of the Commonwealth, or of a State or Territory, to retain or deduct money from money that is
-- or will be owing or payable to the debtor must not retain or deduct money."
-- s 185K(3)(b) and s 185F(1)(c) are not limited to any kind of debt. On their words they also stop a deduction from wages for a
-- child support liability. Encoded literally; see NOTES.md finding 3.
-- Whether a maintenance or proceeds of crime liability is itself a provable debt is not decided here: for the proceedings limbs they
-- are treated as provable (an assumption), and only their enforcement is asserted. A debt incurred after acceptance for processing
-- was recorded is treated as not provable (inference from the s 185 definition of "provable debt").
DECLARE `Debt kind` IS ONE OF
    `an ordinary provable debt`
    `a debt incurred by fraud`
    `a liability under a maintenance agreement or maintenance order`
    `a liability under a proceeds of crime law`
    `a debt incurred after acceptance for processing was recorded`

DECLARE `Creditor action` IS ONE OF
    `enforce a remedy against his person or property`
    `start legal proceedings`
    `take a fresh step in proceedings other than to enforce a judgment`
    `have a sheriff execute court process`
    `retain or deduct money owing to him`

GIVEN `the debt` IS A `Debt kind`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the debt is provable` IF
    CONSIDER `the debt`
    WHEN `a debt incurred after acceptance for processing was recorded` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the debt` IS A `Debt kind`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the debt is frozen` IF
    CONSIDER `the debt`
    WHEN `a liability under a maintenance agreement or maintenance order` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a debt incurred after acceptance for processing was recorded` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the action` IS A `Creditor action`, `the debt` IS A `Debt kind`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a creditor may take the action while the proposal is being processed` IF
    CONSIDER `the action`
    WHEN `enforce a remedy against his person or property` THEN
            (NOT `the debt is frozen` `the debt`)
         OR (`the debt` EQUALS `a liability under a proceeds of crime law`)
    WHEN `start legal proceedings` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `take a fresh step in proceedings other than to enforce a judgment` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `have a sheriff execute court process` THEN NOT `the debt is frozen` `the debt`
    WHEN `retain or deduct money owing to him` THEN FALSE

GIVEN `the action` IS A `Creditor action`, `the debt` IS A `Debt kind`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a creditor may take the action while the agreement is in force` IF
    CONSIDER `the action`
    WHEN `enforce a remedy against his person or property` THEN
            (NOT `the debt is provable` `the debt`)
         OR (`the debt` EQUALS `a liability under a maintenance agreement or maintenance order`)
         OR (`the debt` EQUALS `a liability under a proceeds of crime law`)
    WHEN `start legal proceedings` THEN NOT `the debt is provable` `the debt`
    WHEN `take a fresh step in proceedings other than to enforce a judgment` THEN NOT `the debt is provable` `the debt`
    WHEN `have a sheriff execute court process` THEN NOT `the debt is provable` `the debt`
    WHEN `retain or deduct money owing to him` THEN FALSE

GIVEN `the agreement is in force and on the Index` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a creditor may present or proceed with a creditor's petition` IF
    NOT `the agreement is in force and on the Index`

§§ `185C(2)(d), (e) -- equal ranking and proportionate payment`

-- s 185C(2)(d): the proposal must provide that "all provable debts ... rank equally" and, if the total paid "is insufficient to meet
-- those provable debts in full, those provable debts are to be paid proportionately"; (e) "a creditor is not entitled to receive, in
-- respect of a provable debt, more than the amount of the debt". The administrator's remuneration (s 185C(3A)) is paid in addition
-- and is not modelled.
GIVEN `this creditor's provable debt` IS A NUMBER, `all provable debts` IS A NUMBER, `total paid in respect of provable debts` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`this creditor's share` MEANS
    IF `total paid in respect of provable debts` AT LEAST `all provable debts`
    THEN `this creditor's provable debt`
    ELSE `total paid in respect of provable debts` TIMES `this creditor's provable debt` DIVIDED BY `all provable debts`

§§ `185LB(3), 185LC(3), 185QA -- arrears defaults and termination`

-- s 185LB(3): a 3-month arrears default occurs at the test time if (a) payments became due at the start of the 3-month period ending
-- immediately before it; (b) "throughout that 3-month period, the debtor was in arrears"; and (c) "(i) the total amount that the
-- debtor was so in arrears exceeds $300, or 20% of the total of all of the due payments at the beginning of that 3-month period,
-- whichever is higher; or (ii) if the total of all of the due payments at the beginning of that 3-month period was $300 or less -- no
-- payment was made in that period to reduce any of the due payments". (1): the administrator must notify each creditor within 10
-- business days.
GIVEN `in arrears throughout the 3 months` IS A BOOLEAN, `total arrears` IS A NUMBER, `total due at the start of the 3 months` IS A NUMBER,
      `a payment was made in the period to reduce them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a 3-month arrears default occurs` IF
        `in arrears throughout the 3 months`
    AND (    `total arrears` GREATER THAN `the higher of` 300 (`total due at the start of the 3 months` TIMES 20 DIVIDED BY 100)
          OR (`total due at the start of the 3 months` AT MOST 300 AND (NOT `a payment was made in the period to reduce them`)))

-- s 185LC(3): a designated 6-month arrears default occurs at the test time if "(a) ... (i) before the test time, one or more payments
-- ... became due and payable ...; (ii) at no time during the 6-month period ending immediately before the test time were any
-- obligations in respect of those payments discharged; or (b) ... (i) at the test time, the obligations created by the debt agreement
-- have not been discharged; (ii) the last of those obligations should have been discharged at a time 6 months before the test time".
-- Months are whole months here; "at a time 6 months before" is read as "6 months or more before" (inference).
-- s 185QA: if the administrator notifies and the Official Receiver "is satisfied that the designated 6-month arrears default has
-- occurred", the Official Receiver "must declare in writing that the agreement is terminated" and record it on the Index; it is
-- terminated when recorded. s 185R: "A debt agreement is terminated if the debtor becomes a bankrupt." s 185Q: the Court may also
-- terminate on application of the debtor, a creditor or the Official Receiver, with a sequestration order (not encoded).
GIVEN `a payment had fallen due` IS A BOOLEAN, `months since any obligation for those payments was discharged` IS A NUMBER,
      `all obligations discharged` IS A BOOLEAN, `months since the last obligation fell due` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a designated 6-month arrears default occurs` IF
        (`a payment had fallen due` AND `months since any obligation for those payments was discharged` AT LEAST 6)
    OR  ((NOT `all obligations discharged`) AND `months since the last obligation fell due` AT LEAST 6)

§§ `185M(1D)-(1DB) -- how far a variation may extend the payments`

-- s 185M(1D): a proposal to vary "must not seek to vary the agreement so that the agreement would provide for the debtor to make
-- payments ... after: (a) 3 years beginning on the day the agreement was made; or (b) if subsection (1DA) or (1DB) applies -- 5
-- years". (1DA): s 185C(2AB) applied to the debtor when the proposal was given. (1DB): the administrator certifies reasonable grounds
-- to believe "(i) that the debtor has suffered a substantial change in circumstances after the agreement was made that was not
-- foreseen ...; and (ii) that the debtor is not likely to be able to discharge the obligations ... because of that change"; and "(b)
-- the proposal does not increase the total of the payments".
GIVEN `s 185C(2AB) applied when the proposal was given` IS A BOOLEAN, `the administrator certifies an unforeseen substantial change` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the variation does not increase the total payments` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most years a variation may let payments run` MEANS
    IF     `s 185C(2AB) applied when the proposal was given`
        OR (`the administrator certifies an unforeseen substantial change` AND `the variation does not increase the total payments`)
    THEN 5
    ELSE 3

§§ `185N, 185NA, 153(2) -- the end of the agreement and the release`

-- s 185N(1): "A debt agreement ends when all the obligations that it created have been discharged, unless the agreement has been
-- terminated earlier under section 185P, 185Q, 185QA or 185R." (2): the debtor "is entitled to any property that was subject to the
-- debt agreement but that was not required by the agreement to be distributed to creditors" (Example: Rhea sells her boat and car
-- for $16,000, pays her creditors the $15,000 required, and keeps $1,000). (3): the Official Receiver "must give the debtor a
-- certificate". (5): the administrator notifies the Official Receiver within 5 business days.
-- The Act says nothing about what then stays on the National Personal Insolvency Index, or for how long: the Index, and the
-- matters entered in it, are left to regulations (s 5; s 315(2)(a)-(c)). k075's question is not answered by the Act.
GIVEN `all obligations discharged` IS A BOOLEAN, `terminated earlier under s 185P, 185Q, 185QA or 185R` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the agreement ends under s 185N(1)` IF
    `all obligations discharged` AND (NOT `terminated earlier under s 185P, 185Q, 185QA or 185R`)

GIVEN `realised from the property` IS A NUMBER, `required to be distributed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`what the debtor keeps` MEANS
    IF `realised from the property` GREATER THAN `required to be distributed`
    THEN `realised from the property` MINUS `required to be distributed`
    ELSE 0

-- s 185NA(1): when the agreement ends under s 185N(1), "the debtor is released from provable debts from which the debtor would have
-- been released if the debtor had been discharged from bankruptcy immediately after the acceptance of the relevant debt agreement
-- proposal for processing was recorded". (2): the release ceases if the agreement is declared void. (3): it does not release a joint
-- debtor or a guarantor.
-- s 153(2): discharge does not release (b) "a debt incurred by means of fraud" or (c) "subject to any order of the Court made under
-- subsection (2A)", a liability under a maintenance agreement or maintenance order. s 153 Note: a pecuniary penalty order is not
-- provable (s 82(3A)). A proceeds of crime liability is treated as not released on that note (inference).
GIVEN `the debt` IS A `Debt kind`, `the agreement ended under s 185N(1)` IS A BOOLEAN, `the agreement was declared void` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the debtor is released from the debt` IF
        `the agreement ended under s 185N(1)`
    AND (NOT `the agreement was declared void`)
    AND CONSIDER `the debt`
        WHEN `an ordinary provable debt` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
